Description: headless orchestration harness for authorized security research
 An external LLM (Open WebUI model, gateway or MCP client) semantically
 searches the vector-indexed tool registry (ChromaDB) and executes modules
 with result-projection and budget gates. Python orchestrates; a C plugin
 gates Brain event dispatch; systemd runs the system profile (Brain UDS at
 /run/daharness/brain.sock, state at /var/lib/daharness, config at
 /etc/daharness/daharness.env).
 .
 Privileged lanes (raw sockets, low ports) degrade honestly and are
 documented in daharness-safety(7).
 .
 NOTE: chromadb ships vendored in-package (ledger layer-2 decision);
 python3-mcp
 and python3-pymetasploit3 ride the apt lane pending snapshot-compat
 probes. The Jupyter closure (python3-ipykernel + python3-ipython +
 python3-jupyter-client) is a hard Depends, not the [jupyter] extra:
 without it daharness-kernel.service dies at its lazy import in a
 Restart=on-failure loop (observed 2026-10-20), and Kali rolling builds
 these against the system python (3.14) — the dev pin (6.29.5) predates
 the interpreter the deb lane runs on.